# Round q3gemmb: gemm_q4k's block-step shortened by instructions, bit for bit (leanA2 + nobr + hh +
# ntout). A full-tile warp-step went 889 -> 630/682 instructions (sass_inflight.py --step, hh 0/1);
# registers 128, spill 0. The q3gemmlat model (block-step = instructions x CPI / 2) reads x1.50-1.52
# on the T = 4096 launch; diluted over the window by the report's section G [derived]: pp4096
# 8,009 -> ~9,800 (9,470-9,940), pp512 6,821 -> ~9,430 (8,840-9,430). The same model read x1.15 on
# lever A and the card measured x1.00 (rig-log 09-26#q3gemma-ab), so the band is the model's and the
# lower decisions matter. q3k, q5k and q6k moved too (the shared macro); their bits are gated.
kind: ab
question: does cutting gemm_q4k's warp-step instructions shorten the Qwen3 prompt as the
  instruction-times-CPI model says, where lever A's byte cut did not?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 4096, n = 0, A6000, Qwen3-30B-A3B Q4_K_M - (q3gemmb - base) / base, paired by
  round
unit: %
predict: +18..+24
rounds: 3
condition: this tree's generate_qwen3moe and the base's (the q3fix3 landing it rebases onto, a
  bin: arm) alternate in one lease, BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=3 just depth-gpu-qwen3moe 512
  bin:<base>:512 4096 bin:<base>:4096, the order rotated every round; no row carries
  [other-busy]. The P = 512 rows are read against their own band, +30..+38 %, by the same decisions;
  the decode rows (tg96 at depth 512 and 4096) are a screen for 0 (decode reads no GEMM)
decide-in: land q3gemmb; queue FA next (docs/research/mrsq3-design-report.md: the 1.10x line over
  mistral.rs holds)
decide-below: if the effect is still past the ruler, land it and take one ncu source page of
  gemm_q4k (BLOOMERY_NCU_SOURCE=1) to find the term the model overstated (the loop's i-cache, the
  staging wait); if not, hold it: the model's CPI term was wrong a second time and the design goes
  back before FA
decide-above: land it and re-fit the model's CPI against the measured cycles before FA is specified
